{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794112097,"nonce":"MufmHd/JYeMtdtpU1kbINCaXghw=","message":"As built (514eb0d0), two points differ from the design above. (1) With no GIT_EDITOR, core.editor, VISUAL or EDITOR set, the editor falls back to gitcli's own order (the first of editor, nano, vim, vi, emacs on the PATH, then ed), not straight to vi; gitcli was left as it is. (2) A slow `esc` then `e`: the esc that leaves a text sets a one-key flag on show and new, so a plain `e` right after it counts as `esc e`. Opening and closing the palette right after that esc keeps the flag.","files":null}]}